                <pb facs="0260" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11061: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-06T12:00:00+08:00">August 6,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 6—10:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>670. Legation’s 667, August 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">4</hi>],5 p.m. Following
                    from American Consulate, Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“August 5, 8 p.m. Changsha reported retaken by Ho Chien today. Six
                            regiments of National reinforcements have arrived Hankow today, <pb
                                facs="0261" n="163" xml:id="pg163"/> situation easier. Admiral
                            [Craven] arrived last night. Three American gunboats in Hankow.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
